        "statement": "Assume Countable Choice ([[def-countable-choice]]). Let $H$ be a complex\nHilbert space with a specified norm-dense sequence $(d_j)_{j\\ge1}$, with\ninner product linear in the first argument. Let $A$ be a densely defined\nself-adjoint operator on $H$. There is a unique regular projection-valued\nBorel measure $E$ on $\\mathbb R$ representing $A$, with $E(\\mathbb R)=I$,\nstrong countable additivity, and the exact domain and norm identity\n\n$$D(A)=\\{h:\\int_{\\mathbb R}\\lambda^2d\\mu_h(\\lambda)<\\infty\\},\\qquad \\|Ah\\|^2=\\int\\lambda^2d\\mu_h,\\qquad \\mu_h(B)=\\langle E(B)h,h\\rangle.$$\n\nHere regular means that every finite positive scalar measure $\\mu_h$ is\ninner regular by compact sets and outer regular by open sets. Every bounded\nBorel function $b$ has a uniquely determined bounded operator $b(A)$, with\n$\\|b(A)\\|\\le\\sup|b|$, $(bc)(A)=b(A)c(A)$ and\n$\\overline b(A)=b(A)^*$. Every possibly unbounded complex Borel function\n$b$ has a closed densely defined multiplication realization with exact domain\n$\\{h:\\int|b|^2d\\mu_h<\\infty\\}$ when $b$ is finite valued; its truncations\nconverge on that domain. In particular $e^{itA}$ is a strongly continuous\nunitary group and\n\n$$\\lim_{t\\to0}\\frac{e^{itA}h-h}{t}=iAh\\quad\\Longleftrightarrow\\quad h\\in D(A).$$\n\nRegular representing PVMs and this calculus transport under unitary\nintertwiners. An isometry intertwining the two strongly continuous groups\nhas a reducing closed range and intertwines their PVMs. These conclusions\nuse the specified countable dense sequence and CC, with no general\nAC spectral theorem, Gelfand representation, Riesz-Markov theorem or Stone\nexistence theorem as a premise.",
